        "text": "So how are blocks connected in practice? To answer this question, we need to discuss the concept of hashing. Hashing is the process of using input data of any size to create a fixed size string, which is also called the output, and this is done through mathematical operations known as hash functions. We can use all sorts of input with variable sizes, such as text, images and videos, but the output or the hash will always have a predictable length. The length of the hash depends on the hashing algorithm being used. In other words, hashing consists of taking data of any size and passing it through a function that produces a fixed size hash. In blockchain systems, each block has its own hash that functions as a unique identifier, and every time a new block is created, its hash has to be produced based on the hash of the previous block. So the short answer to our question is blocks are connected through hashes.",
